    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "FUNCTIONS WITH MACROS\n\nMacros are Blueprint's functions: build a chunk of logic once, name it, give it inputs and outputs\nand place it as many times as you like. Open the macro tabs (Clamp, Repeat) next to the\nmain graph to see inside them. Each placed macro is its own copy at compile time, so any state\ninside (a Do Once, a gate) is independent for every call.\nMacro inputs must be WIRED (here from Make Literal nodes), they cannot hold typed-in literals.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          240.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
