          {
            "id": "comment-1",
            "text": "INSIDE THE MACRO\nA macro is a reusable chunk of graph with its own entry and exit. The Entry node (left) exposes the macro's inputs as output pins; the Exit node (right) collects its outputs. Here the exec wire runs straight through, and the value is limited to lo..hi with Clamp (integer) and handed back through the clamped output.",
